---
description: Use when work crosses routers, dependencies, schemas, services, repositories, models, or database access boundaries.
globs: app/**/*.py
---

# Layers

- Keep routers, dependencies, schemas, use cases, services, repositories, domain contracts, and database models in separate modules when the feature has meaningful behavior.
- API owns HTTP shape. Use cases own business scenario orchestration. Domain owns pure rules and contracts. Repositories own persistence. Services own isolated capabilities or integrations. Infrastructure owns technical implementations.
- Apply the focused architecture rule files for the layer being changed:
  - `architecture-api.mdc`
  - `architecture-application.mdc`
  - `architecture-structure.mdc`
  - `architecture-domain.mdc`
  - `architecture-infrastructure.mdc`
  - `architecture-repository.mdc`
  - `architecture-service.mdc`
  - `architecture-use-case.mdc`
  - `architecture-coordination.mdc`
- Shared response and pagination contracts belong under `app/common/responses` and `app/common/pagination`.
- Do not leak SQLAlchemy models directly as API contracts. Convert models to Pydantic response schemas at the boundary.
- Keep repository methods explicit about filters, ordering, limits, and locking. Avoid hidden query behavior.
- Use SQLAlchemy 2 style `select`, `update`, `delete`, typed `Mapped` models, and async sessions.
